id: pmc-rspo
title: Link custom-type items to their registered tracker folders
description: "Custom-type changelog links currently guess lowercase plus s instead of using registered tracker folders. Resolve canonical folders, add real tracker regression coverage and an optional link validity gate. Reported by pm-review PR 9."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-14T13:45:19.109Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T19:40:26.198Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[18]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-14T13:48:13.704Z",codex-agent,"The pinned SDK exposes resolveItemTypeRegistry().type_to_folder, and the same CLI exposes project plus extension definitions through schema list. Use registry-derived itemFolder metadata for custom rows, preserve known built-in folders for standalone inputs, and fail rather than guess unknown custom folders. Add --check-links for generated and prepended tracker links, including root containment."
  "2026-10-14T13:56:18.566Z",codex-agent,"Fleet source audit: pm-review ReviewFinding uses review-findings; pm-rl EvalResult, GateEpisode and MergeOutcome use eval-results, gate-episodes and merge-outcomes; pm-starter StarterNote uses starter-notes. pm-presets AgentRun/Card, pm-ts-starter Spike and pm-web Bug currently resolve to the same folders as the old rule. Current origin/main in pm-vcs and pm-jev has no registered custom folder mismatch. pm-review canonicalFindingLinks remains compatible and becomes redundant after dependency upgrades. The pinned CLI rejects universal list output controls on schema list; the schema call omits those controls."
  "2026-10-14T13:57:21.903Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: restored only the old lowercase-plus-s folder derivation inside toonItemRef, rebuilt dist, then ran node --test test/item-links.test.ts test/custom-types.test.ts. Exit 1: 0/3 passed, 3 failed. The real-tracker path-existence assertion rejected extensionfindings instead of extension-findings; the extension command regression rejected changesets instead of change-records. Restored the implementation and rebuilt dist. Positive focused tests and pm test pmc-rspo --run --progress passed 3/3, with no skips or cancellations."
  "2026-10-14T14:05:33.483Z",codex-agent,"The isolated npm gate passed all 601 tests, with zero failures/skips/cancellations. Coverage found one unexecuted CLI branch: link checking with no explicit pm-cwd. Extended the real tracker test to check the same absolute pm root with the default cwd; thresholds remain unchanged at 100 percent lines, branches and functions. Re-running the complete release gate."
  "2026-10-14T14:13:27.556Z",codex-agent,"Isolated npm release:check passed: 601/601 tests; zero failures, skipped, canceled or todo; 100 percent measured lines/branches/functions across all 13 required source files; 168 documented declarations; zero production audit vulnerabilities. Packaging, dogfood changelog links/drift, release date and publish attestation checks passed. Exact command: env -u PM_PATH -u PM_AUTHOR HOME=$(mktemp -d) GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check. Running the same isolated gate through bun run release:check next."
  "2026-10-14T14:21:08.242Z",codex-agent,"Final delivery gates passed under isolated identity. npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 601/601 tests with zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo and 100 percent measured lines/branches/functions across all 13 required source files. Both production audits reported zero vulnerabilities; docstrings, pack dry-run, dogfood changelog drift/link validation, release date and publish attestation checks passed. Exact isolation prefix for each runner: env -u PM_PATH -u PM_AUTHOR HOME=$(mktemp -d) GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1. Scope remains the registered-folder fix and optional link validation. Consumer dependency bumps and removing the compatible pm-review workaround remain follow-up release work. Releasing the claim without closing the item, then regenerating/checking the package changelog before the SteveBot commit and PR."
  "2026-10-14T14:26:23.060Z",claude-hub,"CodeQL alert 9 (js/polynomial-redos, src/item-links.ts:30) on PR #241: the link-check regex /\\]\\(([^)\\s]+)\\)/g backtracks quadratically on repeated '](!' (measured 161 ms at 5k, 669 ms at 10k, 2748 ms at 20k repetitions). Replaced by markdownLinkTargets(), a single-pass scanner that resumes at the stop character after a failed scan. Test 'link targets match the former regex exactly and stay linear on hostile markdown' checks equivalence against the old regex on 11 edge samples (empty, spaced, nested '](', NBSP, newline, unclosed) and scans 200k repetitions in under 1 s (47 ms). With the old regex restored, that input takes minutes and the bound fails."
  "2026-10-14T15:59:04.262Z",codex-agent,"CodeRabbit round 1 on PR #241: all four findings match the current source. Plan: preserve supplied itemFolder during mixed schema lookup, encode parentheses in generated path segments and ids, parse optional CommonMark titles with a linear scanner, and strip literal query/fragment suffixes before decoding while retaining containment. Each regression will be verified by reverting only the affected function, followed by isolated npm and Bun release gates. No review-thread replies or bot requests."
  "2026-10-14T16:05:12.882Z",codex-agent,"Finding 1 valid and fixed: readPmItems fills only missing itemFolder values. A real CLI wrapper adds archived RemovedType and registered ReviewFinding rows with supplied archives folders alongside custom rows needing schema lookup. Regression: node --test --test-name-pattern='schema lookup preserves' test/item-links.test.ts. Reverted only readPmItems to PR head: exit 1, 0/1 passed, actual folder undefined instead of archives. Restored the function; positive regression passed."
  "2026-10-14T16:05:14.919Z",codex-agent,"Finding 2 valid and fixed: toonItemRef percent-encodes parentheses after encodeURIComponent in every folder segment and item id. Regression: node --test --test-name-pattern='generated links encode parentheses' test/item-links.test.ts; verifies the exact nested path, marked rendering and checkItemLinks against an existing file. Reverted only toonItemRef: exit 1, 0/1 passed, target truncated to reviews(qa instead of the encoded complete path. Restored the function; positive regression passed."
  "2026-10-14T16:05:16.942Z",codex-agent,"Finding 3 valid and fixed: markdownLinkTargets recognises optional double-quoted, single-quoted and parenthesized titles, including escapes. Cached delimiter lookahead bounds each cursor to forward scans and preserves later links after malformed titles. Regression: node --test --test-name-pattern='link checks validate destinations' test/item-links.test.ts. Reverted only markdownLinkTargets: exit 1, 0/1 passed, yielded no target for a titled link. Restored the function; positive regression passed. Extended equivalence cases compare supported titled links with marked; CommonMark disallows unescaped nested parentheses in titles even though marked accepts them. The original 200k hostile input plus three 200k hostile title inputs all scanned together within the 1 s assertion (312 ms in the focused run). No backtracking regex added."
  "2026-10-14T16:05:18.792Z",codex-agent,"Finding 4 valid and fixed: checkItemLinks removes literal query and fragment suffixes before decoding; encoded filename delimiters remain intact and realpath containment remains enforced. Regression: node --test --test-name-pattern='link checks strip literal query' test/item-links.test.ts. Covers suffix order, invalid escapes confined to queries, missing paths, traversal and escaping symlinks. Reverted only checkItemLinks: exit 1, 0/1 passed, existing present.toon#L2 rejected as missing. Restored the function; positive regression passed. All four revert proofs retained the regression tests and other fixes; tests import source so no dist rebuild was needed for these proofs."
  "2026-10-14T16:06:04.870Z",codex-agent,"Restored implementation verification: pm test pmc-rspo --run --progress --match 'node --test test/item-links.test.ts' passed 8/8 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo. The linked command is node --test test/item-links.test.ts test/custom-types.test.ts. Tracker test-result recording is disabled by existing policy, so results are documented here without changing that policy. Initial focused attempts exposed and corrected a wrapper dispatch issue and marked-oracle disagreements outside the supported destination grammar; the final linked run passed. Preparing isolated npm release:check followed by Bun at unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-14T16:09:26.729Z",codex-agent,"Coverage-instrumented adversarial verification exposed excessive instrumentation cost in a single aggregate 1 s assertion for four 200k cases. The final test preserves the original 200k hostile destination and its unchanged 1 s limit; each of three title stress inputs uses 20k repetitions and its own 1 s limit. The instrumented targeted run passed 2/2 (529 ms total). Removed redundant delimiter caching: lookahead stops at a later same-style opener, which must be unescaped because it follows whitespace, so lookahead spans cannot overlap within any of the three styles. This bounds work linearly without a cache branch. Repeated finding 3's function-only revert proof: 0/1 passed, 1 failed; restored targeted title/suffix/adversarial tests passed 3/3. Added built CLI --check-links acceptance for parenthesized paths and a titled missing link in retained prepend history. The first npm gate attempt is superseded; final npm/Bun gates will run on this implementation."
  "2026-10-14T16:16:46.687Z",codex-agent,"Final isolated npm gate passed: pm test pmc-rspo --run --progress --match 'npm run release:check' executed env -u PM_PATH -u PM_AUTHOR HOME=$(mktemp -d) GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check. Results: 606/606 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo; 100 percent measured lines/branches/functions across all 13 required source files; 169 documented declarations across 16 files; zero production vulnerabilities. Typecheck, pack dry-run, changelog drift/link check, release date and publish attestation checks passed. The original 200k hostile input and title stress assertions passed under coverage. Running the matching isolated Bun gate next."
  "2026-10-14T16:17:52.027Z",codex-agent,"Final delivery gates passed on the unchanged implementation: isolated npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 606/606 tests with zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo and 100 percent measured lines/branches/functions across all 13 required source files. Each uses env -u PM_PATH -u PM_AUTHOR HOME=$(mktemp -d) GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 before the runner. Both gates passed typecheck, 169 documented declarations across 16 files, zero production vulnerabilities, pack dry-run, changelog drift/link validation, release date and publish attestation checks. The four findings are valid; each has a focused regression and a function-only revert proof recorded above. PM validation reports zero history drift or chain/hash mismatches across 182 items; existing metadata advisories remain. A shell-expanded scratch identifier in one unpublished comment was rolled back and re-added literally before publication; committed history remains byte-for-byte intact, and added tracked lines contain no private or scratch paths. Baseline PR CodeQL analysis reports zero results and prior alert 9 is fixed. Releasing the claim without closing the item, rebuilding dist and regenerating/checking the changelog before committing and pushing. Final automatic CodeQL will be inspected after the push; no review replies or bot requests."
  "2026-10-20T11:16:54.060Z",codex-agent,"Validation follow-up from pmc-txk1 / PR 262 at code commit 51447ab: the full isolated-HOME/Git Bun release gate ran 682 tests, 670 pass and 12 fail. Eleven are separately tracked readiness failures; the additional failure is the existing test/item-links.test.ts hostile destinations/titles per-input 1000ms wall assertion (whole test duration 1170ms). The identical focused test passes 1/1 without coverage and 1/1 with coverage; the latter whole-test duration is 1797ms across all hostile inputs, with every unchanged per-input bound passing. CI Node 22 and Node 26 each pass all 682 tests on the same source. No scanner, fixture size, assertion or time budget changed. This records an unresolved full-run timing risk without assigning a root cause or claiming a scanner regression."
  "2026-10-21T19:40:26.198Z",codex-agent,"Tracker milestone integration note from PR 265: readTrackerReleaseSnapshot captures the certified full SDK list, whose rows omit itemFolder. The current renderer safely refuses custom-type TOON links without registered folder metadata rather than guessing. Neutral references work by default, and SDK consumers can supply itemTypeFolders explicitly. Include directory-snapshot registry enrichment and milestone CLI custom-folder link coverage when completing this existing follow-up; milestone membership and ordinary notes are independent of physical folders."
